      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since we haven\u0027t needed a value like this up to this point, I might suggest using a different way of keeping your message flow state in the partner emulator to continue not needing this. The Policy Engine has \"ready\" states, during which it is receptive to various kinds of messages. At other times, it is only receptive to expected kinds of messages. I don\u0027t want the partner emulator to be that stateful if we can help it, but it might work to have a state field like `bool ams_in_progress`. (AMS stands for \"atomic message sequence.\")\n\nIf we do need an enum value like this, I would suggest using 0 instead of 32. If someone tries to jam it into an actual PD message, that would still be wrong, but the likely side effects seem easier to debug than 32, which would \"overflow\" the message type field.",
